1
00:00:23,930 --> 00:00:26,230
(Located at the foot of Mount Nam...)

2
00:00:26,230 --> 00:00:29,000
(stands a town with charming alleys.)

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,840
- We're near Shinheung Market.
- Yes.

4
00:00:33,940 --> 00:00:36,540
- Well, Haebangchon...
- We're in Haebangchon.

5
00:00:36,540 --> 00:00:39,680
- We're around Huam-dong.
- Yes.

6
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:40,780
And that's Yongsan.

7
00:00:41,150 --> 00:00:43,320
My goodness. You know what?

8
00:00:43,560 --> 00:00:45,060
This place is amazing.

9
00:00:46,060 --> 00:00:49,030
This whole neighborhood including Haebangchon...

10
00:00:49,130 --> 00:00:50,930
- It's buzzing with people.
- Definitely.

11
00:00:51,260 --> 00:00:54,070
There are so many cafes here. Right?

12
00:00:54,070 --> 00:00:57,370
The guy who's joining us today lives around here.

13
00:00:57,370 --> 00:00:59,640
- He probably lives over there.
- Really?

14
00:00:59,640 --> 00:01:00,940
- Over there?
- Yes.

15
00:01:01,410 --> 00:01:04,040
- I guess you know this guy. I see.
- Yes.

16
00:01:04,040 --> 00:01:05,540
You also know him well.

17
00:01:05,540 --> 00:01:07,380
- Really? Who is it?
- Yes.

18
00:01:07,650 --> 00:01:10,050
You know him very well and like him too.

19
00:01:10,920 --> 00:01:12,690
- Gosh, it's been a while...
- Hello.

20
00:01:12,690 --> 00:01:13,990
since I last saw Jae Seok.

21
00:01:14,990 --> 00:01:16,790
- I'm friends with him?
- Yes.

22
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:19,360
Who is it?

23
00:01:19,930 --> 00:01:22,360
(Jae Seok is clueless.)

24
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:23,600
(They arrive in front of the door.)

25
00:01:23,600 --> 00:01:24,900
Dong Wook lives on the other side of the town.

26
00:01:24,900 --> 00:01:26,800
But his name has the same syllable.

27
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:30,000
Wait. He has a similar name? I see. It's Dong Hwi.

28
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:33,940
(Today's Whenever Friends: Lee Dong Hwi and Yang Se Jong)

29
00:01:34,040 --> 00:01:35,340
- Hello.
- Hello.

30
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:37,040
- Hey. Se Jong.
- Hello.

31
00:01:37,040 --> 00:01:39,380
- Hello.
- It's been a while, Se Jong.

32
00:01:39,810 --> 00:01:40,950
- Se Jong.
- Why are you not coming in?

33
00:01:40,950 --> 00:01:42,480
- Come on in.
- Why are you not coming in?

34
00:01:42,850 --> 00:01:44,680
- Have you been well, Se Jong?
- Yes, I have.

35
00:01:45,150 --> 00:01:46,250
Dong Hwi.

36
00:01:46,250 --> 00:01:48,290
(A tight hug with Yeon Seok)

37
00:01:48,290 --> 00:01:49,390
Dong Hwi.

38
00:01:50,090 --> 00:01:51,990
- Jae Seok.
- Gosh, you look good.

39
00:01:51,990 --> 00:01:54,130
How's your health?

40
00:01:54,290 --> 00:01:57,000
- Come on. There was a follow-up.
- Are you okay?

41
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:58,900
- There was a follow-up article.
- This way.

42
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:02,870
(He steals the scenes whenever he's on the screen.)

43
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,540
Don't say my name.

44
00:02:05,270 --> 00:02:09,510
(He can flawlessly deliver relatable and hilarious performances.)

45
00:02:11,180 --> 00:02:14,550
(But he can also lead the story with his expressive eyes.)

46
00:02:15,510 --> 00:02:19,820
(He exudes a strong presence in every project.)

47
00:02:19,820 --> 00:02:21,020
No one else matters!

48
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:25,390
(Versatile Actor Lee Dong Hwi)

49
00:02:26,130 --> 00:02:31,360
(He played Yeon Seok's rival in "Dr. Romantic.")

50
00:02:33,070 --> 00:02:37,240
(With his handsome looks, he became the national heartthrob.)

51
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:42,810
(He proved that his acting skill outshines his handsome looks.)

52
00:02:43,340 --> 00:02:45,180
You are indeed cruel.

53
00:02:46,110 --> 00:02:49,920
(Yang Se Jong, the actor who never disappoints)

54
00:02:50,150 --> 00:02:51,580
- We're on the show today.
- This is great.

55
00:02:51,580 --> 00:02:53,220
- Dong Hwi and Se Jong...
- This is great.

56
00:02:53,220 --> 00:02:54,820
Wait, didn't you work with Yeon Seok before?

57
00:02:54,820 --> 00:02:56,690
- We're very close.
- I see.

58
00:02:56,920 --> 00:02:59,190
"Dr. Romantic" was his debut project.

59
00:02:59,190 --> 00:03:01,090
- That's right.
- It was his debut project?

60
00:03:01,090 --> 00:03:02,900
- It was ten years ago.
- I see.

61
00:03:02,900 --> 00:03:03,900
Yes.

62
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:06,130
- Ever since then, - Yes.

63
00:03:06,130 --> 00:03:09,300
he's been a very good junior of mine.

64
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,270
- Really?
- He's a different type of junior...

65
00:03:11,270 --> 00:03:12,640
compared to Dong Hwi.

66
00:03:12,640 --> 00:03:13,710
How are they different?

67
00:03:13,710 --> 00:03:15,470
I wouldn't say Dong Hwi is the obedient type.

68
00:03:15,470 --> 00:03:16,780
- Actually, I'm only obedient...
- Well, Dong Hwi is...

69
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,040
to Jae Seok.

70
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:22,210
- I always follow his lead.
- Right.

71
00:03:22,210 --> 00:03:25,150
I already mentioned this several times.

72
00:03:25,150 --> 00:03:27,250
- We met at a commercial shoot.
- I see.

73
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:28,250
You guys met there?

74
00:03:28,250 --> 00:03:29,590
- I was an extra back then.
- Right.

75
00:03:29,590 --> 00:03:31,090
- Oh, back then?
- Yes.

76
00:03:31,090 --> 00:03:34,890
But the thing is, Dong Hwi's career took off 2 or 3 months later.

77
00:03:34,890 --> 00:03:36,700
- His career took off right away.
- I see.

78
00:03:36,700 --> 00:03:38,060
I didn't know he'd get famous that fast.

79
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:40,300
When we were filming "Dr. Romantic,"

80
00:03:40,300 --> 00:03:42,400
I knew he would have a good career.

81
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:43,740
It only took a year for him to get the lead role.

82
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,240
- He got the lead role fast.
- Yes.

83
00:03:45,670 --> 00:03:46,970
- Back then...
- It's all thanks to Yeon Seok.

84
00:03:46,970 --> 00:03:48,040
- Really?
- My gosh, no.

85
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,980
- I learned a lot from him.
- What did you learn from him?

86
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:52,650
- He's such a cool guy.
- Okay.

87
00:03:52,650 --> 00:03:54,180
(Embarrassed)

88
00:03:54,550 --> 00:03:56,050
You're being vague.

89
00:03:56,520 --> 00:03:58,520
- Sure, he's a cool guy.
- I mean it.

90
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:00,620
- You're a bit hesitant.
- No.

91
00:04:00,620 --> 00:04:03,590
- No.
- Everyone's cool. Dong Hwi too.

92
00:04:04,390 --> 00:04:06,330
- Right.
- He's flustered...

93
00:04:06,430 --> 00:04:08,530
- to go into detail.
- My gosh.

94
00:04:08,990 --> 00:04:10,930
- Se Jong and I worked together.
- I'm sorry.

95
00:04:10,930 --> 00:04:11,930
What was the project?

96
00:04:11,930 --> 00:04:13,470
- We filmed "Low Life" together.
- It's "Low Life."

97
00:04:13,470 --> 00:04:14,770
- Right.
- Yes.

98
00:04:14,770 --> 00:04:17,040
- I watched "Low Life."
- That's right.

99
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:18,870
I heard filming "Low Life" wasn't easy for them.

100
00:04:18,870 --> 00:04:19,870
(They became close over hard times.)

101
00:04:19,870 --> 00:04:20,870
- I bet.
- Yes.

102
00:04:21,110 --> 00:04:24,040
Did you recently film another project together?

103
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:27,210
No. From what I heard, we were invited because...

104
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:28,950
- Just because...
- we're close to you guys.

105
00:04:28,950 --> 00:04:30,020
(They were invited without an agenda.)

106
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,180
- We're close to you guys.
- Because you're close...

107
00:04:31,180 --> 00:04:32,380
- You're here as our friends?
- We were just invited.

108
00:04:32,380 --> 00:04:34,720
I think they invited our treasured juniors.

109
00:04:34,720 --> 00:04:35,850
- That's right.
- Yes.

110
00:04:35,850 --> 00:04:39,690
I wondered if they invited me because I lived nearby.

111
00:04:40,060 --> 00:04:41,960
You know what? You look much better these days.

112
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,860
I was going to see you today. So I shaved.

113
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:45,860
- That's great. You look neat.
- Yes.

114
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:47,330
He looks great today.

115
00:04:47,330 --> 00:04:48,800
(Looking his absolute best)

116
00:04:48,800 --> 00:04:50,300
- Your play is over, right?
- Yes.

117
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:52,610
The play you came to watch is over now.

118
00:04:52,610 --> 00:04:54,010
- I'm preparing...
- There's a new play?

119
00:04:54,010 --> 00:04:55,310
- a new play.
- When will it start?

120
00:04:55,310 --> 00:04:58,280
It will premiere on October 25.

121
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:01,450
I've been practicing diligently for the new play titled "The Fall."

122
00:05:01,450 --> 00:05:02,850
A lot of people came to watch him.

123
00:05:02,850 --> 00:05:05,120
Right. That's not an easy thing to pull off these days.

124
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:07,690
But he came to watch when another actor was performing, not me.

125
00:05:08,250 --> 00:05:09,790
I watched another actor perform.

126
00:05:09,790 --> 00:05:10,790
(He went to watch Yoon Na Moo's performance.)

127
00:05:10,790 --> 00:05:11,860
After he watched the play,

128
00:05:11,860 --> 00:05:15,430
he followed us to our get-together. He sat at the next table.

129
00:05:15,890 --> 00:05:17,630
- Listen.
- He wasn't with our crew.

130
00:05:17,630 --> 00:05:19,930
- He loves get-togethers.
- He... Right.

131
00:05:19,930 --> 00:05:21,600
- He also followed his students...
- Listen.

132
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:22,770
- to the retreat.
- I...

133
00:05:22,770 --> 00:05:24,900
- Right. He's a professor.
- He's a professor now.

134
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:25,900
(This professor loves get-togethers.)

135
00:05:25,900 --> 00:05:27,740
Why did you go there? Read the room!

136
00:05:28,210 --> 00:05:30,610
- I didn't follow them there.
- He likes that.

137
00:05:30,610 --> 00:05:33,050
- I was invited to join them.
- Right. You're the professor.

138
00:05:33,050 --> 00:05:35,510
As for their get-together, I wasn't invited.

139
00:05:35,510 --> 00:05:36,720
You went because you wanted to.

140
00:05:39,450 --> 00:05:42,090
- I'll go and watch yours.
- It made me sad.

141
00:05:42,090 --> 00:05:43,920
We should go and watch it. Se Jong.

142
00:05:43,920 --> 00:05:45,290
You must've known him for a long time.

143
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:47,890
- He called you the other day.
- It's been ten years.

144
00:05:47,890 --> 00:05:49,560
- I did.
- Right?

145
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:52,870
Se Jong told the writers that he wouldn't tell anyone...

146
00:05:52,870 --> 00:05:55,870
he was going to join our show and keep it a secret.

147
00:05:55,870 --> 00:05:57,940
But when he and I were talking on the phone...

148
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,710
- He told you?
- They talk often.

149
00:05:59,710 --> 00:06:02,170
- Yes.
- It made me feel guilty.

150
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:04,910
- I see.
- We're very close.

151
00:06:04,910 --> 00:06:06,250
It felt like I should tell him.

152
00:06:06,980 --> 00:06:08,610
- So I told him.
- Good.

153
00:06:08,610 --> 00:06:09,920
- Yeon Seok...
- Dong Hwi wouldn't tell me.

154
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:12,520
I couldn't call Jae Seok.

155
00:06:12,520 --> 00:06:15,390
I mean, I didn't. First of all,

156
00:06:15,390 --> 00:06:17,420
- after the cold incident, - You always follow instructions.

157
00:06:17,990 --> 00:06:19,690
- I thought I should be careful.
- Listen.

158
00:06:19,690 --> 00:06:22,130
- I'm sure...
- What? "Cold incident?"

159
00:06:22,230 --> 00:06:24,330
- he got calls...
- You didn't want to worry him?

160
00:06:24,330 --> 00:06:26,730
- from everyone he knew.
- That's right.

161
00:06:26,730 --> 00:06:28,600
My gosh. The cold incident?

162
00:06:29,330 --> 00:06:30,870
Well, things did snowball.

163
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,340
It wasn't a serious illness.

164
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:35,110
Se Jong, didn't you say you were in Japan?

165
00:06:35,110 --> 00:06:36,510
Yes. I did an event in Japan.

166
00:06:36,510 --> 00:06:37,780
- A fanmeet?
- Yes.

167
00:06:37,780 --> 00:06:40,110
- I didn't know you did that.
- He's very popular in Japan.

168
00:06:40,110 --> 00:06:41,110
Gosh, no.

169
00:06:41,110 --> 00:06:42,380
What did you do at the fanmeet?

170
00:06:42,380 --> 00:06:43,650
- Me?
- Yes.

171
00:06:43,650 --> 00:06:45,520
- I sang.
- You sang?

172
00:06:45,650 --> 00:06:46,920
- What song?
- What did you sing?

173
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:48,990
I sang "On the Street" by Kim Kwang Seok.

174
00:06:49,690 --> 00:06:51,260
Your voice...

175
00:06:51,260 --> 00:06:52,760
- It suits the song.
- suits the song.

176
00:06:52,760 --> 00:06:54,490
Yes. I bet it was a nice fit.

177
00:06:54,490 --> 00:06:57,000
- Your voice sounds a bit husky.
- Well,

178
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:59,630
I also caught the flu last week.

179
00:06:59,630 --> 00:07:02,270
There was another cold incident.

180
00:07:02,270 --> 00:07:04,140
- He also...
- But there were no news articles.

181
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:06,240
- No one knew about it.
- So...

182
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:08,810
if I were home, there wouldn't have been articles.

183
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:11,880
- It was the day of our shoot.
- Right.

184
00:07:11,880 --> 00:07:13,010
Did the fan-meet go well?

185
00:07:13,010 --> 00:07:14,750
I just sang without sparing my voice.

186
00:07:17,150 --> 00:07:18,250
You should.

187
00:07:18,250 --> 00:07:20,190
- Of course. I think I did.
- So you didn't mess up the notes?

188
00:07:21,320 --> 00:07:24,990
It's okay. I'm sure your fans loved the unpolished version of the song.

189
00:07:24,990 --> 00:07:27,530
Are you a good singer, Se Jong?

190
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:29,060
- I'm not a good singer.
- You're not?

191
00:07:29,730 --> 00:07:30,760
I'm really not.

192
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:31,760
(Choking up)

193
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:32,870
We weren't going to ask you to sing.

194
00:07:35,100 --> 00:07:36,700
- Right. So...
- He's already nervous...

195
00:07:36,700 --> 00:07:38,340
- in case we ask him to sing.
- If he doesn't want to...

196
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:40,570
He hurriedly said no while drinking it.

197
00:07:41,070 --> 00:07:42,540
- So...
- "No."

198
00:07:43,510 --> 00:07:44,510
Great.

199
00:07:44,510 --> 00:07:46,080
- He's sweating.
- Right, he's sweating a lot.

200
00:07:46,080 --> 00:07:47,250
As soon as he brought up his singing...

201
00:07:47,250 --> 00:07:48,810
- Are you still sick?
- Did you not recover?

202
00:07:48,810 --> 00:07:50,280
- Maybe not.
- He's still sick.

203
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,620
It's pretty cool today. What's going on?

204
00:07:53,190 --> 00:07:55,250
- Today...
- Sometimes, you feel a bit off.

205
00:07:55,320 --> 00:07:57,860
- Yes.
- No need to feel nervous, Se Jong.

206
00:07:57,860 --> 00:07:59,760
We won't ask you to sing.

207
00:08:00,930 --> 00:08:02,660
(On the street)

208
00:08:02,660 --> 00:08:04,660
(The streetlamp)

209
00:08:05,130 --> 00:08:07,730
- We're not going to ask you.
- Well, he sang first.

210
00:08:07,730 --> 00:08:08,730
All right. Great job.

211
00:08:08,730 --> 00:08:10,970
(He's shy, but still does everything he's asked.)

212
00:08:11,640 --> 00:08:13,140
- I agree.
- Yes.

213
00:08:13,140 --> 00:08:15,770
- Let's check where we're going.
- Okay. We are...

214
00:08:15,770 --> 00:08:17,280
- We're in Haebangchon.
- in Haebangchon.

215
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:18,310
(Where will they spend their first spare time?)

216
00:08:18,710 --> 00:08:19,980
There are so many cards.

217
00:08:20,510 --> 00:08:22,180
All right. Here's the first one.

218
00:08:23,220 --> 00:08:24,720
They have unique names.

219
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:27,620
- Gyul and Fato.
- What?

220
00:08:28,150 --> 00:08:31,920
"My mother gave birth to another carbon copy of me."

221
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:34,930
"And we're making our own hometown here in Haebangchon."

222
00:08:34,930 --> 00:08:36,060
They must be twins.

223
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:40,500
"We've been perfect partners to each other for 30 years."

224
00:08:40,500 --> 00:08:43,540
"And I love spending my days with my younger sister."

225
00:08:43,540 --> 00:08:46,810
"But why does she keep saying that she's disappointed?"

226
00:08:48,810 --> 00:08:50,710
- It sounds like...
- They must be twins.

227
00:08:50,710 --> 00:08:52,380
- they're twins.
- They look identical.

228
00:08:52,380 --> 00:08:53,610
- Right.
- So...

229
00:08:53,610 --> 00:08:54,950
Why is she disappointed?

230
00:08:55,110 --> 00:08:56,920
Younger siblings are always disappointed.

231
00:08:56,920 --> 00:08:58,280
- It's always the case.
- I guess so.

232
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:00,720
- Dong Hwi is an only child.
- Right.

233
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:01,950
He's an only child. What about you, Se Jong?

234
00:09:01,950 --> 00:09:04,560
- I'm also an only child.
- Both of you are only children.

235
00:09:04,560 --> 00:09:06,990
- You guys have that in common.
- Right.

236
00:09:06,990 --> 00:09:08,560
We're similar in some ways.

237
00:09:08,560 --> 00:09:11,000
Do you like spending time...

238
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:14,370
with older people because you're an only child?

239
00:09:14,370 --> 00:09:15,730
- That's part of it.
- I see.

240
00:09:16,670 --> 00:09:18,300
Se Jong especially likes spending time with me...

241
00:09:18,300 --> 00:09:20,570
and treats me like his brother.

242
00:09:20,570 --> 00:09:22,980
- I'm only like this around you.
- Really?

243
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:25,040
- He's not friendly to everyone.
- I guess not.

244
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:26,650
- I really like him.
- Right.

245
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,450
They really like each other. I...

246
00:09:28,450 --> 00:09:30,980
