- That's all that matters.
- When it comes to acting...

495
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:45,210
- That's good.
- He went to the best school.

496
00:17:45,210 --> 00:17:47,580
The letter said that you were a bit disappointed...

497
00:17:47,580 --> 00:17:50,010
in your sister.

498
00:17:50,010 --> 00:17:51,020
Right.

499
00:17:51,020 --> 00:17:52,320
What are you disappointed about?

500
00:17:52,450 --> 00:17:55,820
Well, I've been living in Korea for three years.

501
00:17:55,820 --> 00:17:58,920
I still didn't get to do what I wanted to do with her.

502
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:02,090
It's such an easy thing. Pictures.

503
00:18:02,660 --> 00:18:03,860
- She wants to take pictures...
- Pictures.

504
00:18:03,860 --> 00:18:04,930
- in a photo booth.
- That's right.

505
00:18:04,930 --> 00:18:06,100
You never got to do that?

506
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:08,430
- Never?
- We've taken pictures together.

507
00:18:08,570 --> 00:18:10,400
The problem is that she wants to take them only with me.

508
00:18:10,570 --> 00:18:12,070
Whenever we're about to take the pictures,

509
00:18:12,070 --> 00:18:14,210
my friends end up in the pictures.

510
00:18:14,570 --> 00:18:16,440
We've never done that, just the two of us.

511
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:18,140
(She must be disappointed then.)

512
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:19,640
- She's disappointed about that.
- We couldn't.

513
00:18:19,640 --> 00:18:21,980
You guys can't spend time, just the two of you.

514
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:25,850
But my friends take such good care of her.

515
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:27,590
I...

516
00:18:27,590 --> 00:18:30,190
They do that because they pity me.

517
00:18:30,520 --> 00:18:33,890
(The younger sister's sad counter-argument)

518
00:18:34,430 --> 00:18:36,390
- Because... That's right.
- She doesn't spend time with you.

519
00:18:36,390 --> 00:18:38,400
We still haven't gone on a picnic...

520
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:40,370
- to the Han River.
- Really?

521
00:18:40,530 --> 00:18:43,000
- Yes.
- Well, the thing is,

522
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:45,170
- she's running a business.
- She has a business to run.

523
00:18:45,170 --> 00:18:46,940
- Do you guys live apart?
- No.

524
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:48,640
- You guys live together?
- Yes.

525
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:50,210
Then...

526
00:18:50,210 --> 00:18:51,740
- You guys could've done that then.
- I know.

527
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:55,580
But I make sure that we have tea together.

528
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:56,750
We have it together every night.

529
00:18:56,750 --> 00:18:58,650
- But...
- She has a lot to say.

530
00:18:58,980 --> 00:19:00,690
She has a lot to say.

531
00:19:00,890 --> 00:19:02,250
That's just our culture.

532
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:06,020
It's one of the things we must do every day.

533
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:08,030
- Having tea together. That's...
- I see. Having tea together...

534
00:19:08,490 --> 00:19:10,060
That's not spending time together.

535
00:19:10,060 --> 00:19:12,100
- It's just part of our culture.
- Wait.

536
00:19:12,100 --> 00:19:13,900
Does she not pay you?

537
00:19:14,330 --> 00:19:17,200
I treat her very well here.

538
00:19:17,200 --> 00:19:19,140
- Right?
- Are you happy here?

539
00:19:19,140 --> 00:19:20,870
- Are you happy here?
- I am.

540
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:22,540
(The intonation packs a lot of meaning.)

541
00:19:22,540 --> 00:19:24,840
- She must pay her sister well.
- I...

542
00:19:24,840 --> 00:19:26,510
Of course. Her sister is her boss.

543
00:19:26,510 --> 00:19:27,910
- I'm sure she pays her sister well.
- Right.

544
00:19:27,910 --> 00:19:30,150
- She said it in a weird way.
- We have to go home together.

545
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:31,520
I'm very happy here.

546
00:19:31,850 --> 00:19:33,520
She's living with me.

547
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:34,620
Is that so?

548
00:19:34,790 --> 00:19:35,890
She has to watch what she says.

549
00:19:36,820 --> 00:19:40,290
I ran a bar in Itaewon for over five years.

550
00:19:40,290 --> 00:19:41,830
- That's right.
- Yes. I know.

551
00:19:41,830 --> 00:19:43,230
- I've been there.
- She's been running the cafe...

552
00:19:43,230 --> 00:19:44,660
for four years.

553
00:19:44,660 --> 00:19:46,330
- That's impressive.
- This is the time...

554
00:19:46,330 --> 00:19:48,030
when she must have a lot on her mind.

555
00:19:48,030 --> 00:19:49,930
- Right.
- The contract...

556
00:19:49,930 --> 00:19:53,070
- usually lasts five years.
- That's right.

557
00:19:53,400 --> 00:19:55,740
She might be thinking about whether or not to extend the contract.

558
00:19:55,740 --> 00:19:56,910
- Right.
- You must be thinking...

559
00:19:56,910 --> 00:19:58,080
- about this.
- I...

560
00:19:58,080 --> 00:19:59,510
- How is it for you?
- I thought a lot about it.

561
00:19:59,510 --> 00:20:02,480
Our main dish is kaymak.

562
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:03,950
- Oh, kaymak.
- Kaymak?

563
00:20:03,950 --> 00:20:06,320
We make kaymak from scratch.

564
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:08,320
- It's a famous Turkish dessert.
- Yes.

565
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:09,390
Kaymak.

566
00:20:09,390 --> 00:20:11,990
We opened this cafe because we wanted to sell kaymak.

567
00:20:11,990 --> 00:20:14,030
- Can we taste some?
- It was something we wanted to do.

568
00:20:14,490 --> 00:20:15,760
Hey.

569
00:20:15,990 --> 00:20:17,700
- It's too early for that.
- We're not here for that.

570
00:20:17,700 --> 00:20:19,400
- You can't ask for kaymak.
- Well, kaymak...

571
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:22,870
Jae Seok, you have to wait in line to eat kaymak.

572
00:20:22,870 --> 00:20:24,640
- Right. That's...
- We didn't reserve it in advance.

573
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,900
But can we taste some?

574
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:28,110
- I don't know if I should say it.
- Sure.

575
00:20:28,410 --> 00:20:29,810
We put aside some kaymak for you.

576
00:20:29,810 --> 00:20:31,010
She put it aside for us.

577
00:20:31,710 --> 00:20:33,480
- Then can we taste it?
- You can give it to us.

578
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:35,410
- Really? Are you sure?
- Yes. You can give it to us.

579
00:20:35,410 --> 00:20:36,650
- It's in the fridge.
- Yes.

580
00:20:37,480 --> 00:20:39,580
- Well, kaymak...
- I was curious about kaymak.

581
00:20:39,580 --> 00:20:41,590
- is a Turkish dessert.
- Yes.

582
00:20:41,590 --> 00:20:43,490
It's a must-try dessert when you go to Turkiye.

583
00:20:43,490 --> 00:20:46,760
My family ran a kaymak business for 50 years.

584
00:20:46,760 --> 00:20:49,030
- It's not easy to make this, right?
- It's not.

585
00:20:49,030 --> 00:20:50,730
How do you make kaymak?

586
00:20:50,730 --> 00:20:52,330
That's the secret.

587
00:20:53,970 --> 00:20:55,400
- So...
- I can't tell you that.

588
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,900
(Maintaining ironclad security)

589
00:20:57,900 --> 00:21:00,610
She sounded like Granny Ma Bok Lim.

590
00:21:01,170 --> 00:21:02,210
- She...
- Not even...

591
00:21:02,210 --> 00:21:03,210
- her daughter-in-law knows.
- Right.

592
00:21:03,310 --> 00:21:04,710
She said it in an old commercial.

593
00:21:05,210 --> 00:21:06,810
"Not even my daughter-in-law knows the secret."

594
00:21:07,350 --> 00:21:09,550
It's not just like that in Korea.

595
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:11,350
It's common in Turkiye too.

596
00:21:11,350 --> 00:21:12,550
"That's the secret."

597
00:21:12,550 --> 00:21:13,590
Only my sister knows.

598
00:21:13,590 --> 00:21:15,620
Only my sister knows the secret.

599
00:21:15,620 --> 00:21:19,160
Have it with honey. Put some kaymak on the bread first.

600
00:21:19,160 --> 00:21:20,290
Then honey...

601
00:21:20,860 --> 00:21:22,860
- Should I do that for everyone?
- Sure.

602
00:21:23,430 --> 00:21:26,030
- Is this a good amount?
- It might taste too rich.

603
00:21:26,030 --> 00:21:28,330
- Just spread moderately. Wait.
- I thought it was alcohol.

604
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,070
I've never had kaymak.

605
00:21:30,070 --> 00:21:31,470
- Right. Same here.
- No way.

606
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,940
You'll find the flavor unique if you haven't had it.

607
00:21:34,470 --> 00:21:36,440
It's different from cheese.

608
00:21:36,440 --> 00:21:38,540
- It's different.
- It's also different from butter.

609
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:40,480
- Right.
- On our menu,

610
00:21:40,480 --> 00:21:42,810
- it's called "real kaymak."
- Really?

611
00:21:42,880 --> 00:21:44,080
- It's really authentic.
- I see.

612
00:21:44,450 --> 00:21:45,820
You know everything, Yeon Seok.

613
00:21:45,820 --> 00:21:47,850
This is good. Turkiye...

614
00:21:48,390 --> 00:21:49,650
- Gosh.
- is famous for this.

615
00:21:50,590 --> 00:21:51,890
This is so good. Try it.

616
00:21:52,220 --> 00:21:53,760
- It tastes rich and sweet.
- Let me try it too.

617
00:21:53,760 --> 00:21:55,160
- Kids love it.
- Oh, my.

618
00:21:55,360 --> 00:21:56,630
- It's healthy too.
- Gosh, this is...

619
00:21:56,630 --> 00:21:57,800
(Wide-eyed)

620
00:21:58,330 --> 00:21:59,730
We have a lot of leftover milk...

621
00:21:59,730 --> 00:22:01,500
- This is so good.
- after we make kaymak.

622
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:03,470
We give it out to our regular customers' dogs...

623
00:22:03,700 --> 00:22:05,170
- with the bread.
- You give it out to them?

624
00:22:06,240 --> 00:22:07,940
(Amazed)

625
00:22:07,940 --> 00:22:09,970
- It's so savory.
- Goodness.

626
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:12,640
- Jae Seok.
- My gosh, it's...

627
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:14,010
Even the bread is good.

628
00:22:14,180 --> 00:22:16,350
- We make the bread ourselves.
- It's good.

629
00:22:16,450 --> 00:22:17,880
- It's really good.
- The scary part about kaymak...

630
00:22:18,250 --> 00:22:19,420
is that once you start eating it,

631
00:22:19,420 --> 00:22:20,690
- You keep going back for more.
- you just...

632
00:22:20,920 --> 00:22:24,090
We have to make a fresh batch every morning.

633
00:22:24,090 --> 00:22:26,420
It's because you don't add any preservatives, right?

634
00:22:26,420 --> 00:22:29,760
But your younger sister is the one who normally makes it, right?

635
00:22:29,890 --> 00:22:31,760
It's such a hassle for me.

636
00:22:31,960 --> 00:22:33,200
To be honest.

637
00:22:34,570 --> 00:22:36,770
- No, it takes a long time.
- How honest of you.

638
00:22:36,770 --> 00:22:39,770
I taught her how to make it, and now she's better at it than I am.

639
00:22:39,770 --> 00:22:41,940
- She nags at me whenever I make it.
- It's delicious.

640
00:22:42,340 --> 00:22:43,810
- Why are you wagging your finger?
- Listen.

641
00:22:43,810 --> 00:22:46,710
Whenever I do something well, my sister is like,

642
00:22:46,810 --> 00:22:50,620
"You're good at it. You should make it from now on."

643
00:22:50,750 --> 00:22:53,350
That's how I ended up getting good at everything.

644
00:22:55,590 --> 00:22:57,260
You weren't good at it from the beginning.

645
00:22:57,620 --> 00:22:58,620
- Exactly.
- But you ended up...

646
00:22:58,620 --> 00:22:59,620
being good at it all.

647
00:22:59,620 --> 00:23:00,630
Yes.

648
00:23:01,360 --> 00:23:02,560
The older sister can see...

649
00:23:02,560 --> 00:23:03,760
- the big picture.
- Right?

650
00:23:03,760 --> 00:23:06,330
- Yes, I do everything with a plan.
- Wait.

651
00:23:08,230 --> 00:23:09,500
They've really picked up...

652
00:23:09,500 --> 00:23:10,870
- those Korean vibes.
- That's right.

653
00:23:10,900 --> 00:23:13,570
Anyway, we enjoyed...

654
00:23:13,570 --> 00:23:16,510
the food you two served us.

655
00:23:16,510 --> 00:23:18,210
- It's our turn to return the favor.
- Of course.

656
00:23:18,210 --> 00:23:19,940
Let's give it a shot.

657
00:23:20,950 --> 00:23:23,580
All right, starting with Round One.

658
00:23:23,720 --> 00:23:24,780
- There's a piece of paper inside.
- I...

659
00:23:24,780 --> 00:23:26,680
- Please read it out loud.
- Will I be able to?

660
00:23:26,680 --> 00:23:28,590
- Give me a minute.
- We have to do well.

661
00:23:28,590 --> 00:23:30,120
- Okay, I can read it.
- Good luck to us.

662
00:23:30,720 --> 00:23:34,260
"For that long-awaited first outing with my sister,"

663
00:23:34,490 --> 00:23:36,060
- "five..."
- "Five-star."

664
00:23:36,060 --> 00:23:37,230
Right, five-star. Sorry.

665
00:23:37,660 --> 00:23:39,530
"Make it a five-star buffet with a view!"

666
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:42,200
- "Grand..."
- "Grand Hyatt Hotel..."

667
00:23:42,200 --> 00:23:44,270
- It's nearby.
- "buffet dining voucher..."

668
00:23:44,270 --> 00:23:46,500
- "for 2."
- Dining voucher for 2?

669
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:48,940
- Dining voucher for two.
- You could even walk there.

670
00:23:48,940 --> 00:23:51,140
- Yes, - Just take a stroll.

671
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:52,580
it's a 15-minute walk from here.

672
00:23:52,580 --> 00:23:53,950
We can totally walk there.

673
00:23:53,950 --> 00:23:55,480
- You could walk there.
- The place is amazing.

674
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:56,910
(Ping-pong Cheers!)

675
00:23:56,910 --> 00:23:59,820
(Bounce ping-pong balls into four glasses.)

676
00:23:59,820 --> 00:24:02,490
(Round 1: 4 cocktail glasses)

677
00:24:02,590 --> 00:24:04,720
(5 balls provided)

678
00:24:04,890 --> 00:24:06,890
- While sitting down?
- While we all sit down?

679
00:24:08,030 --> 00:24:09,060
How...

680
00:24:09,360 --> 00:24:10,760
Isn't it about bouncing the balls in?

681
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:12,960
- Yes, correct.
- Right?

682
00:24:14,070 --> 00:24:15,200
So it's...

683
00:24:15,200 --> 00:24:16,270
(Back-to-back scores)

684
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:19,240
- Jae Seok's great at it.
- I'm not half bad, am I?

685
00:24:19,600 --> 00:24:21,410
I'm on a roll these days.

686
00:24:21,810 --> 00:24:24,110
(Impressed)

687
00:24:25,480 --> 00:24:27,310
All good. I'm all set.

688
00:24:28,210 --> 00:24:29,450
- I've got it.
- Right?

689
00:24:29,450 --> 00:24:31,550
- I'm good.
- I'm good too.

690
00:24:32,050 --> 00:24:33,580
- This one's tough.
- Do we just need to get...

691
00:24:33,580 --> 00:24:34,720
- one ball in each glass?
- This is so...

692
00:24:34,990 --> 00:24:36,250
- One each?
- Yes.

693
00:24:36,550 --> 00:24:38,760
- But 1 person can get 2 balls.
- Correct.

694
00:24:39,290 --> 00:24:40,490
It's a tough one.

695
00:24:40,490 --> 00:24:41,830
The game isn't easy.

696
00:24:41,860 --> 00:24:44,960
If we clear Round One, that'd be amazing.

697
00:24:44,960 --> 00:24:46,430
I feel like it'll go in, but it doesn't.

698
00:24:46,700 --> 00:24:48,130
Getting balls into all four glasses...

699
00:24:48,130 --> 00:24:49,800
- in one attempt will be hard.
- It's hard.

700
00:24:50,070 --> 00:24:51,140
Okay.

701
00:24:51,640 --> 00:24:54,240
I'm good.

702
00:24:55,470 --> 00:24:57,240
- I'm all good.
- It's so slippery.

703
00:24:57,440 --> 00:24:58,510
Things are looking bright.

704
00:25:00,010 --> 00:25:01,850
(Dong Hwi also practices.)

705
00:25:01,850 --> 00:25:03,820
- That's it.
- I've got it.

706
00:25:04,880 --> 00:25:06,020
- I've got it.
- Right.

707
00:25:06,020 --> 00:25:07,490
- I'm good.
- I'm good too.

708
00:25:07,490 --> 00:25:09,050
If someone misses,

709
00:25:09,050 --> 00:25:11,220
- let's give them the extra ball.
- Okay.

710
00:25:11,220 --> 00:25:12,260
- Let's do that.
- Okay.

711
00:25:12,360 --> 00:25:14,490
Then one player gets to go twice,

712
00:25:14,660 --> 00:25:16,190
- and the others get to go once.
- All good.

713
00:25:16,190 --> 00:25:17,800
- Shall we give it a go?
- Yes.

714
00:25:18,100 --> 00:25:20,670
Let's go counterclockwise.

715
00:25:20,670 --> 00:25:22,630
- Sounds good. Okay.
- First to last.

716
00:25:22,630 --> 00:25:24,040
- Let's do a group cheer.
- Go.

717
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:26,100
- In 1, 2, 3. Go!
- Go!

718
00:25:28,040 --> 00:25:29,470
- Here we go.
- Here we go.

719
00:25:29,470 --> 00:25:30,510
Here we go.

720
00:25:30,510 --> 00:25:37,980
(Out of 10 total tries, they're on try number 1.)

721
00:25:39,350 --> 00:25:40,380
See?

722
00:25:40,550 --> 00:25:42,420
(The first ball is wasted just like that.)

723
00:25:42,790 --> 00:25:43,790
Jae Seok.

724
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:46,620
- Jae Seok...
- It's not...

725
00:25:46,620 --> 00:25:49,430
- We haven't failed.
- Jae Seok has another ball.

726
00:25:49,760 --> 00:25:51,760
- You have four balls left.
- I'll take my turn.

727
00:25:51,760 --> 00:25:52,930
- I...
- I must succeed.

728
00:25:52,930 --> 00:25:55,670
I suddenly feel the pressure now that it's the real deal.

729
00:25:56,230 --> 00:25:58,870
- I told you.
- I was so good at it earlier.

730
00:25:59,870 --> 00:26:01,310
Gosh, I'm getting goosebumps.

731
00:26:01,310 --> 00:26:03,210
(1st try)

732
00:26:03,210 --> 00:26:04,280
Nice.

733
00:26:05,110 --> 00:26:07,210
- You're amazing at it.
- Dong Hwi, good luck.

734
00:26:07,210 --> 00:26:08,510
(3rd player, Dong Hwi)

735
00:26:10,650 --> 00:26:11,920
- Is this okay?
- Yes.

736
00:26:13,350 --> 00:26:15,220
(The ball went into the glass in front of Jae Seok.)

737
00:26:17,460 --> 00:26:18,690
Can't we switch seats?

738
00:26:19,390 --> 00:26:21,630
(Only the glass in front of Dong Hwi remains!)

739
00:26:21,630 --> 00:26:23,090
- We can switch seats, right?
- Yes.

740
00:26:23,090 --> 00:26:24,430
- No?
- No?

741
00:26:25,600 --> 00:26:26,730
That's bad.

742
00:26:27,000 --> 00:26:28,570
