- And a quesadilla?

1424
00:50:25,736 --> 00:50:27,366
Okay. My goodness.

1425
00:50:27,366 --> 00:50:28,506
That was easy.

1426
00:50:28,976 --> 00:50:30,106
That's right.

1427
00:50:30,606 --> 00:50:31,706
What is that?

1428
00:50:32,806 --> 00:50:34,616
I put in some tissues because I sweated so much before.

1429
00:50:34,616 --> 00:50:35,746
- Really?
- Yes.

1430
00:50:36,216 --> 00:50:37,446
You got them ready.

1431
00:50:38,086 --> 00:50:41,686
- You can't help but adore him.
- I agree.

1432
00:50:42,116 --> 00:50:44,086
When he's with older guys, he listens to them carefully.

1433
00:50:44,316 --> 00:50:45,486
When he's with younger ones,

1434
00:50:45,486 --> 00:50:47,556
- he's very manly. Yes.
- He has leadership.

1435
00:50:47,686 --> 00:50:49,096
He's very loyal too.

1436
00:50:49,096 --> 00:50:51,566
He's the type of younger friend I love the most.

1437
00:50:52,066 --> 00:50:53,896
- He sticks to one thing.
- That's right.

1438
00:50:53,896 --> 00:50:54,966
He focuses on one thing only.

1439
00:50:55,096 --> 00:50:57,766
We've witnessed him focusing on one thing several times.

1440
00:50:58,636 --> 00:51:00,436
- We pulled it off because of you.
- That's right.

1441
00:51:00,436 --> 00:51:02,876
I rode the momentum as soon as he threw the ball.

1442
00:51:02,936 --> 00:51:04,276
That was really interesting.

1443
00:51:04,446 --> 00:51:06,276
You threw it by feel, and the ball was already in there.

1444
00:51:06,276 --> 00:51:07,816
- The thick cup wasn't an easy one.
- It was already in the cup.

1445
00:51:07,816 --> 00:51:10,616
No. I can't do well when people are paying attention.

1446
00:51:11,146 --> 00:51:13,446
- It bounced.
- I did it when no one cared.

1447
00:51:13,846 --> 00:51:16,656
When we go to our next spot,

1448
00:51:16,786 --> 00:51:18,286
let's go for Round Three.

1449
00:51:18,286 --> 00:51:19,926
- Of course.
- Let's get a clear win.

1450
00:51:19,926 --> 00:51:22,026
- It's been a while.
- Let's do it as it's been a while.

1451
00:51:22,796 --> 00:51:24,126
It's not that hot...

1452
00:51:24,126 --> 00:51:25,896
- It's great.
- after it stopped raining.

1453
00:51:25,896 --> 00:51:27,166
It's perfect.

1454
00:51:27,196 --> 00:51:28,596
- What? Is that gomtang...
- It's so nice.

1455
00:51:28,596 --> 00:51:29,666
across the street?

1456
00:51:30,036 --> 00:51:32,066
(All of a sudden?)

1457
00:51:32,066 --> 00:51:34,776
Jae Seok. Aren't you being too fickle?

1458
00:51:35,506 --> 00:51:38,176
Sorry. I tend to do that.

1459
00:51:38,176 --> 00:51:40,246
It's interesting that when we have foreign food,

1460
00:51:40,246 --> 00:51:42,716
- we crave Korean food.
- We do that a little. Gosh.

1461
00:51:42,716 --> 00:51:44,176
- Here's your quesadilla.
- Okay.

1462
00:51:44,176 --> 00:51:45,316
Thank you.

1463
00:51:46,416 --> 00:51:48,186
(On the smoky meat,)

1464
00:51:48,186 --> 00:51:51,256
(they add lots of cheese and sauce.)

1465
00:51:51,256 --> 00:51:52,686
They fried the tortillas so that they're crunchy...

1466
00:51:52,686 --> 00:51:54,256
- like dumplings.
- That's right.

1467
00:51:54,256 --> 00:51:56,096
I can have them for the first time in a while...

1468
00:51:56,096 --> 00:51:57,896
- because Yeon Shik gave permission.
- Yes.

1469
00:51:58,426 --> 00:51:59,466
It was hard.

1470
00:51:59,466 --> 00:52:01,436
- Okay. Should I try it?
- Sure.

1471
00:52:03,066 --> 00:52:04,196
(Surprised)

1472
00:52:04,196 --> 00:52:05,236
Is it hot?

1473
00:52:05,236 --> 00:52:06,266
